# 01. Purpose

This document defines the API architecture and service boundaries for AEGIS.

It establishes the contract between:

```text
AEGIS FRONTEND
      ↓
APPLICATION/API LAYER
      ↓
DOMAIN SERVICES
      ↓
PERSISTENCE / EVENT INFRASTRUCTURE
```

It defines:

1. API architectural principles
2. API boundaries
3. Query contracts
4. Command contracts
5. Service responsibilities
6. Request/response conventions
7. Error handling
8. Validation
9. Authorization boundaries
10. State transition enforcement
11. Real-time event contracts
12. Idempotency
13. Concurrency
14. Pagination
15. Filtering
16. Search
17. Audit integration
18. Transaction boundaries
19. Frontend integration rules
20. AI coding-agent implementation rules

The objective is simple:

> **The frontend should never have to guess how AEGIS works.**

---

# 02. API Philosophy

AEGIS is a high-stakes operational system.

Therefore the API must prioritize:

```text
Correctness
Traceability
Consistency
Security
Explicitness
Predictability
Observability
```

before convenience.

The API is not merely a transport mechanism for UI data.

It is an enforcement boundary for the AEGIS domain model.

