# 10. Observation Service

## Responsibility

Manages observations entering the AEGIS domain.

It is responsible for:

```text
create observation
validate observation
associate source
associate location
record observation time
record provenance
retrieve observations
```

It must not independently classify a threat.

---

# 11. Signal Service

Responsible for structured signals derived from observations.

Responsibilities:

```text
create signal
associate observations
track signal status
retrieve signals
```

The Signal Service must preserve source lineage.

---

# 12. Anomaly Service

Responsible for anomalies requiring operational attention.

Responsibilities:

```text
create anomaly
associate signals
classify anomaly severity/context
track anomaly status
retrieve anomaly
```

It does not independently declare a confirmed threat.

---

# 13. Event Service

Responsible for operational events.

Responsibilities:

```text
create event
retrieve event
update event state
associate threats
associate evidence
associate locations
```

---

# 14. Threat Service

Responsible for threat-domain operations.

Responsibilities include:

```text
create threat context
retrieve threat
update classification
update confidence
update status
associate evidence
associate investigations
associate risk assessments
```

The Threat Service must enforce threat state transitions.

---

# 15. Risk Service

Responsible for risk assessments.

Responsibilities:

```text
create assessment
retrieve assessment
update assessment
retrieve assessment history
associate evidence
```

Risk assessments must be immutable historical records once finalized where required by governance.

A new assessment may supersede an older one rather than rewriting it.

---

# 16. Investigation Service

Responsible for investigations.

Responsibilities:

```text
start investigation
retrieve investigation
assign actors
add hypotheses
add findings
associate evidence
update investigation status
complete investigation
```

---

# 17. Case Service

Responsible for case-level operational tracking.

Responsibilities:

```text
create case
retrieve case
update case
associate event
associate evidence
associate findings
manage case relationships
```

---

# 18. Finding Service

Responsible for findings generated during investigation.

Responsibilities:

```text
create finding
retrieve finding
update finding where permitted
associate evidence
associate investigation
```

A finding must retain traceability to its evidence.

---

# 19. Transmission Service

Responsible for structured transmission assessments.

Responsibilities:

```text
create assessment
update assessment
associate source
associate target
associate pathway
associate evidence
update confidence
```

The service must preserve uncertainty.

---

# 20. Containment Service

Responsible for containment actions.

Responsibilities:

```text
propose containment
retrieve containment
authorize containment
execute containment
verify containment
cancel containment
record outcome
```

Containment actions must follow the canonical state machine.

---

# 21. Response Service

Responsible for broader response activities.

Responsibilities:

```text
create response
start response
update response
complete response
record outcome
```

A response may contain or reference multiple containment actions.

---

# 22. Recovery Service

Responsible for recovery assessments.

Responsibilities:

```text
start recovery assessment
record observations
associate evidence
evaluate recovery
confirm recovery
```

Recovery confirmation must not be equivalent to manually changing a status field.

---

# 23. Preparedness Service

Responsible for institutional learning.

Responsibilities:

```text
create lesson
identify resilience gap
create improvement item
update improvement progress
retrieve preparedness history
```

The service closes the biological feedback loop.

---

# 24. Research Service

Responsible for research findings.

Responsibilities:

```text
create research finding
retrieve research finding
associate source
associate evidence
associate operational entities
```

Research information must remain distinct from operational facts.

---

# 25. Evidence Service

Responsible for evidence metadata and provenance.

Responsibilities:

```text
register evidence
retrieve evidence
associate evidence
record provenance
record integrity metadata
```

The Evidence Service should not determine the operational conclusion derived from evidence.

---

# 26. Notification Service

Responsible for user-facing operational notifications.

Responsibilities:

```text
create notification
retrieve notifications
mark notification read
dismiss notification where permitted
```

Notifications should reference domain events or entities.

---

# 27. Audit Service

Responsible for immutable or append-oriented audit records.

Responsibilities:

```text
record consequential action
record actor
record entity
record previous state
record resulting state
record reason
record timestamp
```

The audit layer must not depend on the UI.

---

# 28. Real-Time Service

Responsible for distributing approved domain events.

Responsibilities:

```text
subscribe client
publish domain event
filter authorized events
deliver update
handle reconnection
```

It must not become a second source of domain truth.

