# 29. Query Architecture

Queries should be optimized around user needs.

Conceptually:

```text
UI SCREEN
 ↓
QUERY
 ↓
QUERY SERVICE
 ↓
DOMAIN / PROJECTION
 ↓
RESPONSE
```

The query layer may aggregate multiple domain entities.

Example:

```text
Threat Overview
 ↓
Threat
 + Risk Assessment
 + Evidence
 + Investigation
 + Actions
```

This does not mean those entities become one database entity.

---

# 30. Command Architecture

Commands represent intent.

Example:

```text
START_INVESTIGATION
```

rather than:

```text
UPDATE_INVESTIGATION_STATUS = "active"
```

The command allows the domain to determine whether the transition is valid.

---

# 31. Command Processing Contract

Every consequential command follows:

```text
REQUEST
 ↓
AUTHENTICATE
 ↓
AUTHORIZE
 ↓
VALIDATE
 ↓
CHECK CURRENT STATE
 ↓
CHECK DOMAIN RULES
 ↓
EXECUTE
 ↓
PERSIST
 ↓
EMIT EVENT
 ↓
AUDIT
 ↓
RETURN RESULT
```

No shortcut is permitted.

