# 33. Collection Query Contract

Collection endpoints support:

```text
pagination
filtering
sorting
search
time range
location
status
severity
```

where applicable.

Example conceptual request:

```text
GET /api/v1/threats
  ?status=under_review
  &severity=high
  &locationId=LOC-001
  &page=1
  &pageSize=25
```

The final query vocabulary must be defined per resource.

---

# 34. Pagination

Collection responses should use explicit pagination metadata.

Conceptually:

```text
{
  "data": [],
  "meta": {
    "page": 1,
    "pageSize": 25,
    "total": 143,
    "totalPages": 6
  }
}
```

The API must not silently return unbounded datasets.

---

# 35. Cursor Pagination

For high-volume real-time or time-ordered datasets, cursor pagination may be preferred.

Conceptually:

```text
?cursor=...
&pageSize=50
```

The choice should be made based on resource behavior rather than applied mechanically.

---

# 36. Filtering

Filters must correspond to canonical domain fields.

Example:

```text
status
severity
location
organization
createdAt
observedAt
updatedAt
```

Frontend-only filter semantics must not contradict backend semantics.

---

# 37. Sorting

Sort fields must be explicitly whitelisted.

Example:

```text
sort=createdAt
sort=-severity
```

The backend must reject unsupported sort fields rather than interpreting arbitrary input.

---

# 38. Search

Search should distinguish:

```text
exact identifier lookup
```

from:

```text
full-text search
```

and:

```text
structured filtering
```

They are not interchangeable.

---

# 39. Resource Detail Contract

A resource detail response should return the canonical entity.

Conceptually:

```text
{
  "data": {
    "id": "...",
    "type": "...",
    ...
  }
}
```

Related information should be explicitly requested or included through a defined expansion mechanism.

---

# 40. Relationship Queries

Relationships should have explicit API semantics.

Examples:

```text
GET /threats/:id/investigations
GET /investigations/:id/findings
GET /investigations/:id/evidence
GET /cases/:id/relationships
GET /events/:id/threats
```

Do not hide critical relationships inside arbitrary nested JSON.

